    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a world-class personal portfolio website for:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nProfessional identity:\nProduct Builder \302\267 Full-Stack Developer \302\267 Founder\n\nBrand affiliation:\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\nIMPORTANT BRAND DISTINCTION:\nThis is Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide\'s PERSONAL portfolio.\n\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED is his umbrella technology brand/company identity.\nNAMACO IS NOT one of his portfolio projects.\n\nDo not place NAMACO inside the project list as if it were a project/client.\nInstead, present it as the technology brand under which Hassan is building.\n\n============================================================\n01 \342\200\224 PRIMARY OBJECTIVE\n============================================================\n\nCreate a premium, highly credible personal portfolio that positions Hassan as:\n\n- a product builder\n- a full-stack developer\n- a founder\n- a technology creator\n- someone who can take an idea from concept to implementation\n\nThe portfolio should appeal to:\n\n- startup founders\n- technology executives\n- CTOs\n- engineering leaders\n- product leaders\n- investors\n- recruiters\n- potential clients\n- technology companies in Africa and globally\n\nThe central message should be:\n\n\"I don\'t just write code.\nI turn ideas into real digital products.\"\n\nThe website must communicate ambition without exaggeration.\n\nDo not fabricate:\n- employment\n- awards\n- clients\n- funding\n- revenue\n- user numbers\n- partnerships\n- certifications\n- testimonials\n- business results\n\nEverything must remain defensible and truthful.\n\n============================================================\n02 \342\200\224 VISUAL DIRECTION\n============================================================\n\nDesign the website as a premium editorial technology portfolio.\n\nThe visual quality should resemble a serious:\n- technology company\n- product studio\n- founder portfolio\n- engineering/product case-study platform\n\nIt must NOT look like:\n- a generic developer portfolio\n- a free website template\n- a coding bootcamp portfolio\n- a \"hacker\" website\n- a cyberpunk website\n- an AI-generated landing page\n- a crypto landing page\n- an over-designed startup template\n\nUse:\n\nPRIMARY VISUAL LANGUAGE\n- black\n- white\n- near-black\n- subtle neutral grays\n\nThe overall aesthetic should feel:\n\n- premium\n- intelligent\n- restrained\n- confident\n- editorial\n- modern\n- precise\n- cinematic\n- sophisticated\n\nTypography is extremely important.\n\nUse:\n- large editorial headlines\n- excellent letter spacing\n- strong typographic hierarchy\n- clean modern sans-serif typography\n- large whitespace\n- sharp grid alignment\n- intentional spacing\n\nMinimalism must not make the website feel empty.\n\nEvery section must have a clear purpose.\n\n============================================================\n03 \342\200\224 OFFICIAL NAMACO BRAND\n============================================================\n\nUse the official NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED logo supplied by the owner.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nUse the logo exactly as supplied.\n\nDO NOT:\n- redesign it\n- redraw it\n- modify the symbol\n- stretch it\n- distort it\n- create another NAMACO logo\n\nNAMACO should appear subtly in the personal portfolio.\n\nPossible placement:\n- footer\n- About section\n- small brand affiliation line\n- navigation or brand system where appropriate\n\nDo not make NAMACO more prominent than Hassan\'s personal identity.\n\n============================================================\n04 \342\200\224 NAVIGATION\n============================================================\n\nCreate a refined sticky navigation.\n\nNavigation:\n\nWORK\nABOUT\nCAPABILITIES\nCONTACT\n\nRight side:\n\nLET\'S CONNECT\n\nKeep navigation minimal.\n\nOn mobile:\nUse a clean full-screen or elegant slide-down navigation.\n\nDo not use a generic hamburger menu with poor styling.\n\n============================================================\n05 \342\200\224 HERO SECTION\n============================================================\n\nThe hero must immediately establish Hassan\'s identity.\n\nDisplay:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nSmall descriptor:\n\nPRODUCT BUILDER\nFULL-STACK DEVELOPER\nFOUNDER\n\nPrimary headline:\n\n\"I build digital products that move ideas forward.\"\n\nAlternative approved headline:\n\n\"I turn ambitious ideas into real digital products.\"\n\nDo NOT use:\n\n\"Hi, I\'m Hassan\"\n\"Welcome to my portfolio\"\n\"I\'m a passionate developer\"\n\"I love coding\"\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n\"I\'m Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 a product builder, full-stack developer, and founder focused on turning ideas into useful digital experiences, platforms, and products.\"\n\nDisplay subtle brand affiliation:\n\n\"Building under NAMACO\"\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\nVIEW SELECTED WORK\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\nLET\'S CONNECT\n\nHero design should use:\n- oversized typography\n- subtle grid\n- precise alignment\n- restrained animation\n- elegant whitespace\n- small metadata/details\n\nDo not use stock photography.\n\nDo not generate a fake portrait.\n\n============================================================\n06 \342\200\224 POSITIONING SECTION\n============================================================\n\nCreate an editorial introduction immediately after the hero.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"From idea to interface to product.\"\n\nCopy:\n\n\"I work across product thinking, interface design, frontend development, backend systems, and deployment \342\200\224 bringing ideas from concept to something people can actually use.\"\n\nCreate a visual transition between the hero and selected work.\n\n============================================================\n07 \342\200\224 SELECTED WORK\n============================================================\n\nThis is the most important section of the website.\n\nSection title:\n\nSELECTED WORK\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"A collection of products, platforms, experiments, and digital experiences I\'ve built.\"\n\nUse large premium case-study cards.\n\nEach project should have:\n- project number\n- name\n- category\n- concise description\n- visual preview\n- technologies where appropriate\n- link\n- case study link if available\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 01 \342\200\224 VEYRA\n============================================================\n\nNAME:\n\nVEYRA\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nPRODUCT \302\267 PLATFORM \302\267 FULL-STACK\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://vetra-waitlist-azure.vercel.app/\n\nDescription:\n\n\"Veyra is a platform concept focused on helping ambitious young builders find the right people to build with and turn ideas into collaborative projects.\"\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT describe Veyra as:\n\"an AI-powered project marketplace.\"\n\nPosition Veyra around:\n- team building\n- collaboration\n- ambitious builders\n- project formation\n- building together\n- product development\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\nSECONDARY CTA:\n\nCASE STUDY\n\nCase study should explain:\n\n01 \342\200\224 Overview\n02 \342\200\224 Problem\n03 \342\200\224 Product Vision\n04 \342\200\224 User Experience\n05 \342\200\224 Design\n06 \342\200\224 Technical Architecture\n07 \342\200\224 Authentication\n08 \342\200\224 Database\n09 \342\200\224 Deployment\n10 \342\200\224 Challenges\n11 \342\200\224 Lessons Learned\n\nOnly include technical details that can be verified from the actual project.\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 02 \342\200\224 DOERLY\n============================================================\n\nNAME:\n\nDOERLY\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nSTARTUP \302\267 PLATFORM \302\267 PRODUCT\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://doerlyai.vercel.app/\n\nDescription:\n\n\"Doerly is a platform built around helping creative people connect, collaborate, and turn ideas into completed work.\"\n\nDo not invent functionality.\n\nFocus on:\n- product vision\n- creative collaboration\n- user experience\n- workflows\n- product decisions\n- implementation\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\nSECONDARY:\n\nCASE STUDY\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 03 \342\200\224 TAHAB HOTEL\n============================================================\n\nNAME:\n\nTAHAB HOTEL & SUITES\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nCLIENT WORK \302\267 HOSPITALITY \302\267 WEB EXPERIENCE\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://tahab-hotel-demo.netlify.app/\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A modern digital experience created for a hospitality brand, focused on presenting the property, experience, and services through a polished web presence.\"\n\nClearly label:\n\nCLIENT / BUSINESS WORK\n\nDo not imply ownership of the hotel.\n\nDo not fabricate hotel metrics or business results.\n\nShow:\n- desktop\n- mobile\n- responsive layout\n- visual design\n- information architecture\n- implementation\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 04 \342\200\224 SPLIT & SETTLE\n============================================================\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://v0-problem-solving-ideas.vercel.app/\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nWEB APP \302\267 PRODUCT EXPERIMENT\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A web application exploring a simple way for groups to record shared expenses and understand who owes what.\"\n\nShow:\n- concept\n- user flow\n- interface\n- implementation\n- product reasoning\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\n============================================================\n08 \342\200\224 MORE WORK\n============================================================\n\nCreate a section after Featured Work:\n\nMORE WORK\n\nThis section should communicate that Hassan has built a broad range of digital experiences.\n\nCreate a premium project grid.\n\nDo not make every project equally large.\n\nUse visual hierarchy.\n\n============================================================\n09 \342\200\224 CLIENT & BUSINESS WORK\n============================================================\n\nCreate a separate category:\n\nCLIENT & BUSINESS WORK\n\nSupporting statement:\n\n\"Digital experiences and technology work created to help businesses establish a stronger presence online.\"\n\nInclude:\n\nQUAFIX PLUGS\n\nADESHINA GADGET\n\nK-TECH\n\nABY GADGETS\n\nSOFTY GADGETS\n\nHIBEE COMPUTER TECHNOLOGY\n\nThese should NOT be presented as startups owned by Hassan.\n\nUse accurate labels such as:\n\n- Website Development\n- Digital Setup\n- Web Experience\n- Business Website\n- Technology Support\n- Design & Development\n\nOnly use the exact contribution once verified.\n\nEach card should include:\n- business name\n- screenshot\n- category\n- Hassan\'s role/contribution\n- link if available\n\n============================================================\n10 \342\200\224 PROJECT FILTERING\n============================================================\n\nAdd a premium filter system.\n\nFILTERS:\n\nALL\nPRODUCTS\nCLIENT WORK\nWEB APPS\nEXPERIMENTS\n\nUse smooth transitions.\n\nFiltering must work properly.\n\nMaintain excellent UX on mobile.\n\n============================================================\n11 \342\200\224 CASE STUDY EXPERIENCE\n============================================================\n\nFor major projects create individual case-study pages.\n\nCase study layout:\n\n01 \342\200\224 OVERVIEW\n\n02 \342\200\224 THE PROBLEM\n\n03 \342\200\224 THE IDEA\n\n04 \342\200\224 PRODUCT THINKING\n\n05 \342\200\224 USER EXPERIENCE\n\n06 \342\200\224 DESIGN\n\n07 \342\200\224 ENGINEERING\n\n08 \342\200\224 KEY DECISIONS\n\n09 \342\200\224 CHALLENGES\n\n10 \342\200\224 OUTCOME\n\n11 \342\200\224 WHAT I LEARNED\n\nDo not invent outcomes.\n\nWhen actual metrics do not exist, be transparent.\n\nExample:\n\n\"Early-stage project focused primarily on product validation and technical execution.\"\n\nHonesty should increase credibility.\n\n============================================================\n12 \342\200\224 ABOUT\n============================================================\n\nCreate a strong editorial About section.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Building from Africa, thinking globally.\"\n\nCopy:\n\n\"I\'m Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide, a Nigerian product builder, full-stack developer, and founder interested in building technology that solves real problems.\n\nI enjoy working across the entire product lifecycle \342\200\224 from figuring out what should be built, to designing the experience, writing the software, connecting the systems, and getting the product into people\'s hands.\n\nMy long-term ambition is to build technology companies from Africa that can compete on a global stage.\"\n\nTone:\n\n- intelligent\n- ambitious\n- grounded\n- honest\n- confident\n- human\n\nDo not make this sound like a motivational speech.\n\n============================================================\n13 \342\200\224 WHAT I BUILD\n============================================================\n\nSection:\n\nWHAT I BUILD\n\nCreate four or five capabilities.\n\nPRODUCT\n\n\"Turning ideas into structured digital products.\"\n\nFRONTEND\n\n\"Responsive, polished interfaces and modern web applications.\"\n\nBACKEND\n\n\"APIs, authentication, databases, business logic, and application architecture.\"\n\nFULL-STACK\n\n\"Connecting product, frontend, backend, data, and deployment.\"\n\nEXPERIMENTS\n\n\"Rapidly testing concepts and building prototypes.\"\n\n============================================================\n14 \342\200\224 TECHNOLOGY\n============================================================\n\nCreate a clean technology section.\n\nUse actual technologies represented in Hassan\'s work.\n\nCurrent technology list may include:\n\nHTML\nCSS\nJAVASCRIPT\nREACT\nVITE\nTAILWIND CSS\nNODE.JS\nEXPRESS\nPOSTGRESQL\nSUPABASE\nREST APIs\nAUTHENTICATION\nGIT\nGITHUB\nVERCEL\nNETLIFY\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nOnly show technologies actually used in the demonstrated work.\n\nDo not add technologies just to make the portfolio look impressive.\n\nTechnology should support the story rather than become the story.\n\n============================================================\n15 \342\200\224 HOW I BUILD\n============================================================\n\nCreate a section:\n\nHOW I BUILD\n\nSTEP 01\nUNDERSTAND\n\n\"Understand the problem, user, business, and desired outcome.\"\n\nSTEP 02\nSTRUCTURE\n\n\"Define the product, information architecture, workflows, and technical requirements.\"\n\nSTEP 03\nDESIGN\n\n\"Create a clear, usable interface and interaction system.\"\n\nSTEP 04\nBUILD\n\n\"Implement the frontend, backend, database, authentication, and integrations.\"\n\nSTEP 05\nSHIP\n\n\"Deploy, test, refine, and make the product usable in the real world.\"\n\nThis section should make it obvious Hassan thinks beyond simply writing code.\n\n============================================================\n16 \342\200\224 PROOF OF WORK\n============================================================\n\nCreate a section:\n\nPROOF OF WORK\n\nShow visual evidence instead of empty claims.\n\nInclude:\n- actual screenshots\n- interface captures\n- responsive layouts\n- product previews\n- selected code snippets where appropriate\n- architecture diagrams\n- workflows\n- deployment evidence\n- project links\n\nThe message should be:\n\n\"I build.\"\n\nNot:\n\n\"I say I can build.\"\n\n============================================================\n17 \342\200\224 CURRENT FOCUS\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nCURRENTLY BUILDING\n\nFeature:\n\nVEYRA\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n\"Exploring better ways for ambitious builders to find the right people, form teams, and build together.\"\n\nSecondary line:\n\n\"Continuing to explore product ideas, full-stack systems, and technology ventures under NAMACO.\"\n\n============================================================\n18 \342\200\224 PERSONAL BRAND / NAMACO CONNECTION\n============================================================\n\nIntroduce NAMACO subtly.\n\nExample:\n\n\"Building with a long-term technology company mindset under NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED.\"\n\nDo not turn the portfolio into a NAMACO corporate website.\n\nThis remains Hassan\'s personal portfolio.\n\n============================================================\n19 \342\200\224 CONTACT\n============================================================\n\nCreate a powerful final CTA.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Let\'s build something meaningful.\"\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"I\'m open to interesting projects, collaborations, product conversations, and opportunities to build.\"\n\nDisplay:\n\nEMAIL\nolamideh825@gmail.com\n\nPHONE\n08051842700\n\nINSTAGRAM\n@namacotechnology\n\nInstagram URL:\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/namacotechnology\n\nUse elegant iconography.\n\nOnly include other social networks when their real URLs are provided.\n\nDo not fabricate GitHub, LinkedIn, X, or other profiles.\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\nSEND AN EMAIL\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\nVIEW INSTAGRAM\n\n============================================================\n20 \342\200\224 FOOTER\n============================================================\n\nFooter:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nPRODUCT BUILDER \302\267 FULL-STACK DEVELOPER \302\267 FOUNDER\n\nBuilding under:\n\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\nFooter navigation:\n\nWORK\nABOUT\nCAPABILITIES\nCONTACT\n\nContact:\n\nolamideh825@gmail.com\n\nPhone:\n\n08051842700\n\nInstagram:\n\n@namacotechnology\n\nAdd:\n\n\302\251 2026 Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide\n\nDo not make the footer unnecessarily large.\n\n============================================================\n21 \342\200\224 MICRO-INTERACTIONS\n============================================================\n\nUse elegant motion.\n\nPreferred:\n- page reveal\n- subtle typography animation\n- smooth scrolling\n- project image reveal\n- card hover states\n- understated image movement\n- navigation transitions\n\nAvoid:\n- excessive particles\n- neon glow\n- bouncing objects\n- giant 3D graphics\n- spinning shapes\n- flashy cursor effects\n- excessive parallax\n\nAnimation should communicate refinement.\n\n============================================================\n22 \342\200\224 RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n============================================================\n\nThe website must be exceptional on:\n\nDESKTOP\nTABLET\nMOBILE\n\nDo not simply collapse desktop into mobile.\n\nMobile must have deliberate:\n- typography\n- spacing\n- navigation\n- image ratios\n- project cards\n- interaction patterns\n- case-study layouts\n\nNo horizontal overflow.\n\nNo broken layouts.\n\nNo tiny unreadable text.\n\n============================================================\n23 \342\200\224 ACCESSIBILITY\n============================================================\n\nImplement:\n\n- semantic HTML\n- keyboard navigation\n- visible focus states\n- correct heading hierarchy\n- accessible buttons\n- descriptive alt text\n- sufficient contrast\n- accessible navigation\n- reduced-motion support\n\n============================================================\n24 \342\200\224 PERFORMANCE\n============================================================\n\nBuild a production-quality website.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- optimized images\n- lazy loading\n- responsive images\n- semantic markup\n- efficient React architecture\n- minimal unnecessary JavaScript\n- fast initial load\n- clean component structure\n- no unnecessary libraries\n- no console errors\n- no broken links\n\n============================================================\n25 \342\200\224 SEO\n============================================================\n\nPage title:\n\nHassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 Product Builder, Full-Stack Developer & Founder\n\nMeta description:\n\n\"Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide is a Nigerian product builder, full-stack developer, and founder building digital products, platforms, and technology experiences.\"\n\nOpen Graph title:\n\nHassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 Product Builder & Founder\n\nOpen Graph description:\n\n\"Digital products, platforms, experiments, and technology experiences built by Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide.\"\n\nUse clean URLs.\n\nExample:\n\n/\n/work\n/work/veyra\n/work/doerly\n/work/tahab-hotel\n/work/split-and-settle\n/about\n/contact\n\n============================================================\n26 \342\200\224 PROJECT CARD DESIGN\n============================================================\n\nProject cards should feel editorial and premium.\n\nEach card should include:\n\nPROJECT NUMBER\n\nPROJECT NAME\n\nCATEGORY\n\nSHORT DESCRIPTION\n\nVISUAL\n\nYEAR\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\nExample:\n\n01\n\nVEYRA\n\nPRODUCT \302\267 PLATFORM\n\n\"Helping ambitious builders find the right people to build with.\"\n\n2026\n\nVIEW PROJECT \342\206\222\n\nProject images should dominate the card.\n\nUse actual screenshots rather than generic generated illustrations.\n\n============================================================\n27 \342\200\224 VISUAL STORYTELLING\n============================================================\n\nDo not make the website text-heavy.\n\nLet the work speak visually.\n\nUse large:\n- product screenshots\n- browser previews\n- mobile mockups\n- UI crops\n- interface details\n\nFor each important project, create a visual narrative.\n\nThe visitor should be able to understand the quality of the work before reading every paragraph.\n\n============================================================\n28 \342\200\224 PERSONAL POSITIONING\n============================================================\n\nThe portfolio must establish this identity:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nis not presented merely as:\n\n\"someone learning to code.\"\n\nHe is presented as:\n\nA young technology builder who is actively creating products, learning by building, working with businesses, and developing toward becoming a serious founder.\n\nThis positioning must come from the actual portfolio evidence.\n\nDo NOT fabricate seniority.\n\nDo NOT call Hassan:\n- senior engineer\n- CTO\n- billionaire founder\n- industry leader\n- expert in every technology\n\nunless those claims become factually justified.\n\nAmbition is enough.\n\n============================================================\n29 \342\200\224 FINAL EXPERIENCE\n============================================================\n\nThe visitor\'s mental progression should be:\n\nFIRST:\n\n\"Who is this?\"\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\nProduct Builder \302\267 Full-Stack Developer \302\267 Founder\n\nTHEN:\n\n\"What has he actually built?\"\n\nVEYRA\nDOERLY\nTAHAB HOTEL\nSPLIT & SETTLE\nCLIENT WORK\nMORE PROJECTS\n\nTHEN:\n\n\"Does he understand technology?\"\n\nFrontend\nBackend\nDatabase\nAuthentication\nDeployment\nProduct Architecture\n\nTHEN:\n\n\"Does he understand products?\"\n\nProblem\nProduct\nDesign\nEngineering\nShipping\n\nFINALLY:\n\n\"What could he build next?\"\n\nCurrently Building:\nVEYRA\n\nBuilding under:\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\n============================================================\n30 \342\200\224 CRITICAL DESIGN PRINCIPLE\n============================================================\n\nBuild a portfolio where the WORK is the proof.\n\nLess self-promotion.\nMore evidence.\n\nLess:\n\"I\'m passionate about technology.\"\n\nMore:\n\"Here is what I built.\"\n\nLess:\n\"I am a great developer.\"\n\nMore:\n\"Here is the product, architecture, interface, and implementation.\"\n\nLess decoration.\nMore precision.\n\nLess template.\nMore identity.\n\nThe final website must feel:\n\nPREMIUM\nINTELLIGENT\nTECHNICAL\nAMBITIOUS\nCREDIBLE\nEDITORIAL\nHUMAN\nUNMISTAKABLY HASSAN\n\nThe final impression should be:\n\n\"This person is still early in his journey, but he is already building seriously.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"He doesn\'t just write code.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"He thinks about products.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"I want to see what he builds next.\"\n\n============================================================\nFINAL PERSONAL INFORMATION\n============================================================\n\nFULL NAME:\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nROLE:\nProduct Builder \302\267 Full-Stack Developer \302\267 Founder\n\nBRAND:\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\nEMAIL:\nolamideh825@gmail.com\n\nPHONE:\n08051842700\n\nINSTAGRAM:\n@namacotechnology\n\nINSTAGRAM URL:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/namacotechnology"
    items {
      text: "Build a world-class personal portfolio website for:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nProfessional identity:\nProduct Builder \302\267 Full-Stack Developer \302\267 Founder\n\nBrand affiliation:\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\nIMPORTANT BRAND DISTINCTION:\nThis is Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide\'s PERSONAL portfolio.\n\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED is his umbrella technology brand/company identity.\nNAMACO IS NOT one of his portfolio projects.\n\nDo not place NAMACO inside the project list as if it were a project/client.\nInstead, present it as the technology brand under which Hassan is building.\n\n============================================================\n01 \342\200\224 PRIMARY OBJECTIVE\n============================================================\n\nCreate a premium, highly credible personal portfolio that positions Hassan as:\n\n- a product builder\n- a full-stack developer\n- a founder\n- a technology creator\n- someone who can take an idea from concept to implementation\n\nThe portfolio should appeal to:\n\n- startup founders\n- technology executives\n- CTOs\n- engineering leaders\n- product leaders\n- investors\n- recruiters\n- potential clients\n- technology companies in Africa and globally\n\nThe central message should be:\n\n\"I don\'t just write code.\nI turn ideas into real digital products.\"\n\nThe website must communicate ambition without exaggeration.\n\nDo not fabricate:\n- employment\n- awards\n- clients\n- funding\n- revenue\n- user numbers\n- partnerships\n- certifications\n- testimonials\n- business results\n\nEverything must remain defensible and truthful.\n\n============================================================\n02 \342\200\224 VISUAL DIRECTION\n============================================================\n\nDesign the website as a premium editorial technology portfolio.\n\nThe visual quality should resemble a serious:\n- technology company\n- product studio\n- founder portfolio\n- engineering/product case-study platform\n\nIt must NOT look like:\n- a generic developer portfolio\n- a free website template\n- a coding bootcamp portfolio\n- a \"hacker\" website\n- a cyberpunk website\n- an AI-generated landing page\n- a crypto landing page\n- an over-designed startup template\n\nUse:\n\nPRIMARY VISUAL LANGUAGE\n- black\n- white\n- near-black\n- subtle neutral grays\n\nThe overall aesthetic should feel:\n\n- premium\n- intelligent\n- restrained\n- confident\n- editorial\n- modern\n- precise\n- cinematic\n- sophisticated\n\nTypography is extremely important.\n\nUse:\n- large editorial headlines\n- excellent letter spacing\n- strong typographic hierarchy\n- clean modern sans-serif typography\n- large whitespace\n- sharp grid alignment\n- intentional spacing\n\nMinimalism must not make the website feel empty.\n\nEvery section must have a clear purpose.\n\n============================================================\n03 \342\200\224 OFFICIAL NAMACO BRAND\n============================================================\n\nUse the official NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED logo supplied by the owner.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nUse the logo exactly as supplied.\n\nDO NOT:\n- redesign it\n- redraw it\n- modify the symbol\n- stretch it\n- distort it\n- create another NAMACO logo\n\nNAMACO should appear subtly in the personal portfolio.\n\nPossible placement:\n- footer\n- About section\n- small brand affiliation line\n- navigation or brand system where appropriate\n\nDo not make NAMACO more prominent than Hassan\'s personal identity.\n\n============================================================\n04 \342\200\224 NAVIGATION\n============================================================\n\nCreate a refined sticky navigation.\n\nNavigation:\n\nWORK\nABOUT\nCAPABILITIES\nCONTACT\n\nRight side:\n\nLET\'S CONNECT\n\nKeep navigation minimal.\n\nOn mobile:\nUse a clean full-screen or elegant slide-down navigation.\n\nDo not use a generic hamburger menu with poor styling.\n\n============================================================\n05 \342\200\224 HERO SECTION\n============================================================\n\nThe hero must immediately establish Hassan\'s identity.\n\nDisplay:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nSmall descriptor:\n\nPRODUCT BUILDER\nFULL-STACK DEVELOPER\nFOUNDER\n\nPrimary headline:\n\n\"I build digital products that move ideas forward.\"\n\nAlternative approved headline:\n\n\"I turn ambitious ideas into real digital products.\"\n\nDo NOT use:\n\n\"Hi, I\'m Hassan\"\n\"Welcome to my portfolio\"\n\"I\'m a passionate developer\"\n\"I love coding\"\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n\"I\'m Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 a product builder, full-stack developer, and founder focused on turning ideas into useful digital experiences, platforms, and products.\"\n\nDisplay subtle brand affiliation:\n\n\"Building under NAMACO\"\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\nVIEW SELECTED WORK\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\nLET\'S CONNECT\n\nHero design should use:\n- oversized typography\n- subtle grid\n- precise alignment\n- restrained animation\n- elegant whitespace\n- small metadata/details\n\nDo not use stock photography.\n\nDo not generate a fake portrait.\n\n============================================================\n06 \342\200\224 POSITIONING SECTION\n============================================================\n\nCreate an editorial introduction immediately after the hero.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"From idea to interface to product.\"\n\nCopy:\n\n\"I work across product thinking, interface design, frontend development, backend systems, and deployment \342\200\224 bringing ideas from concept to something people can actually use.\"\n\nCreate a visual transition between the hero and selected work.\n\n============================================================\n07 \342\200\224 SELECTED WORK\n============================================================\n\nThis is the most important section of the website.\n\nSection title:\n\nSELECTED WORK\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"A collection of products, platforms, experiments, and digital experiences I\'ve built.\"\n\nUse large premium case-study cards.\n\nEach project should have:\n- project number\n- name\n- category\n- concise description\n- visual preview\n- technologies where appropriate\n- link\n- case study link if available\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 01 \342\200\224 VEYRA\n============================================================\n\nNAME:\n\nVEYRA\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nPRODUCT \302\267 PLATFORM \302\267 FULL-STACK\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://vetra-waitlist-azure.vercel.app/\n\nDescription:\n\n\"Veyra is a platform concept focused on helping ambitious young builders find the right people to build with and turn ideas into collaborative projects.\"\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT describe Veyra as:\n\"an AI-powered project marketplace.\"\n\nPosition Veyra around:\n- team building\n- collaboration\n- ambitious builders\n- project formation\n- building together\n- product development\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\nSECONDARY CTA:\n\nCASE STUDY\n\nCase study should explain:\n\n01 \342\200\224 Overview\n02 \342\200\224 Problem\n03 \342\200\224 Product Vision\n04 \342\200\224 User Experience\n05 \342\200\224 Design\n06 \342\200\224 Technical Architecture\n07 \342\200\224 Authentication\n08 \342\200\224 Database\n09 \342\200\224 Deployment\n10 \342\200\224 Challenges\n11 \342\200\224 Lessons Learned\n\nOnly include technical details that can be verified from the actual project.\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 02 \342\200\224 DOERLY\n============================================================\n\nNAME:\n\nDOERLY\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nSTARTUP \302\267 PLATFORM \302\267 PRODUCT\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://doerlyai.vercel.app/\n\nDescription:\n\n\"Doerly is a platform built around helping creative people connect, collaborate, and turn ideas into completed work.\"\n\nDo not invent functionality.\n\nFocus on:\n- product vision\n- creative collaboration\n- user experience\n- workflows\n- product decisions\n- implementation\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\nSECONDARY:\n\nCASE STUDY\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 03 \342\200\224 TAHAB HOTEL\n============================================================\n\nNAME:\n\nTAHAB HOTEL & SUITES\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nCLIENT WORK \302\267 HOSPITALITY \302\267 WEB EXPERIENCE\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://tahab-hotel-demo.netlify.app/\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A modern digital experience created for a hospitality brand, focused on presenting the property, experience, and services through a polished web presence.\"\n\nClearly label:\n\nCLIENT / BUSINESS WORK\n\nDo not imply ownership of the hotel.\n\nDo not fabricate hotel metrics or business results.\n\nShow:\n- desktop\n- mobile\n- responsive layout\n- visual design\n- information architecture\n- implementation\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\n============================================================\nPROJECT 04 \342\200\224 SPLIT & SETTLE\n============================================================\n\nLIVE URL:\n\nhttps://v0-problem-solving-ideas.vercel.app/\n\nCATEGORY:\n\nWEB APP \302\267 PRODUCT EXPERIMENT\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A web application exploring a simple way for groups to record shared expenses and understand who owes what.\"\n\nShow:\n- concept\n- user flow\n- interface\n- implementation\n- product reasoning\n\nCTA:\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\n============================================================\n08 \342\200\224 MORE WORK\n============================================================\n\nCreate a section after Featured Work:\n\nMORE WORK\n\nThis section should communicate that Hassan has built a broad range of digital experiences.\n\nCreate a premium project grid.\n\nDo not make every project equally large.\n\nUse visual hierarchy.\n\n============================================================\n09 \342\200\224 CLIENT & BUSINESS WORK\n============================================================\n\nCreate a separate category:\n\nCLIENT & BUSINESS WORK\n\nSupporting statement:\n\n\"Digital experiences and technology work created to help businesses establish a stronger presence online.\"\n\nInclude:\n\nQUAFIX PLUGS\n\nADESHINA GADGET\n\nK-TECH\n\nABY GADGETS\n\nSOFTY GADGETS\n\nHIBEE COMPUTER TECHNOLOGY\n\nThese should NOT be presented as startups owned by Hassan.\n\nUse accurate labels such as:\n\n- Website Development\n- Digital Setup\n- Web Experience\n- Business Website\n- Technology Support\n- Design & Development\n\nOnly use the exact contribution once verified.\n\nEach card should include:\n- business name\n- screenshot\n- category\n- Hassan\'s role/contribution\n- link if available\n\n============================================================\n10 \342\200\224 PROJECT FILTERING\n============================================================\n\nAdd a premium filter system.\n\nFILTERS:\n\nALL\nPRODUCTS\nCLIENT WORK\nWEB APPS\nEXPERIMENTS\n\nUse smooth transitions.\n\nFiltering must work properly.\n\nMaintain excellent UX on mobile.\n\n============================================================\n11 \342\200\224 CASE STUDY EXPERIENCE\n============================================================\n\nFor major projects create individual case-study pages.\n\nCase study layout:\n\n01 \342\200\224 OVERVIEW\n\n02 \342\200\224 THE PROBLEM\n\n03 \342\200\224 THE IDEA\n\n04 \342\200\224 PRODUCT THINKING\n\n05 \342\200\224 USER EXPERIENCE\n\n06 \342\200\224 DESIGN\n\n07 \342\200\224 ENGINEERING\n\n08 \342\200\224 KEY DECISIONS\n\n09 \342\200\224 CHALLENGES\n\n10 \342\200\224 OUTCOME\n\n11 \342\200\224 WHAT I LEARNED\n\nDo not invent outcomes.\n\nWhen actual metrics do not exist, be transparent.\n\nExample:\n\n\"Early-stage project focused primarily on product validation and technical execution.\"\n\nHonesty should increase credibility.\n\n============================================================\n12 \342\200\224 ABOUT\n============================================================\n\nCreate a strong editorial About section.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Building from Africa, thinking globally.\"\n\nCopy:\n\n\"I\'m Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide, a Nigerian product builder, full-stack developer, and founder interested in building technology that solves real problems.\n\nI enjoy working across the entire product lifecycle \342\200\224 from figuring out what should be built, to designing the experience, writing the software, connecting the systems, and getting the product into people\'s hands.\n\nMy long-term ambition is to build technology companies from Africa that can compete on a global stage.\"\n\nTone:\n\n- intelligent\n- ambitious\n- grounded\n- honest\n- confident\n- human\n\nDo not make this sound like a motivational speech.\n\n============================================================\n13 \342\200\224 WHAT I BUILD\n============================================================\n\nSection:\n\nWHAT I BUILD\n\nCreate four or five capabilities.\n\nPRODUCT\n\n\"Turning ideas into structured digital products.\"\n\nFRONTEND\n\n\"Responsive, polished interfaces and modern web applications.\"\n\nBACKEND\n\n\"APIs, authentication, databases, business logic, and application architecture.\"\n\nFULL-STACK\n\n\"Connecting product, frontend, backend, data, and deployment.\"\n\nEXPERIMENTS\n\n\"Rapidly testing concepts and building prototypes.\"\n\n============================================================\n14 \342\200\224 TECHNOLOGY\n============================================================\n\nCreate a clean technology section.\n\nUse actual technologies represented in Hassan\'s work.\n\nCurrent technology list may include:\n\nHTML\nCSS\nJAVASCRIPT\nREACT\nVITE\nTAILWIND CSS\nNODE.JS\nEXPRESS\nPOSTGRESQL\nSUPABASE\nREST APIs\nAUTHENTICATION\nGIT\nGITHUB\nVERCEL\nNETLIFY\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nOnly show technologies actually used in the demonstrated work.\n\nDo not add technologies just to make the portfolio look impressive.\n\nTechnology should support the story rather than become the story.\n\n============================================================\n15 \342\200\224 HOW I BUILD\n============================================================\n\nCreate a section:\n\nHOW I BUILD\n\nSTEP 01\nUNDERSTAND\n\n\"Understand the problem, user, business, and desired outcome.\"\n\nSTEP 02\nSTRUCTURE\n\n\"Define the product, information architecture, workflows, and technical requirements.\"\n\nSTEP 03\nDESIGN\n\n\"Create a clear, usable interface and interaction system.\"\n\nSTEP 04\nBUILD\n\n\"Implement the frontend, backend, database, authentication, and integrations.\"\n\nSTEP 05\nSHIP\n\n\"Deploy, test, refine, and make the product usable in the real world.\"\n\nThis section should make it obvious Hassan thinks beyond simply writing code.\n\n============================================================\n16 \342\200\224 PROOF OF WORK\n============================================================\n\nCreate a section:\n\nPROOF OF WORK\n\nShow visual evidence instead of empty claims.\n\nInclude:\n- actual screenshots\n- interface captures\n- responsive layouts\n- product previews\n- selected code snippets where appropriate\n- architecture diagrams\n- workflows\n- deployment evidence\n- project links\n\nThe message should be:\n\n\"I build.\"\n\nNot:\n\n\"I say I can build.\"\n\n============================================================\n17 \342\200\224 CURRENT FOCUS\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nCURRENTLY BUILDING\n\nFeature:\n\nVEYRA\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n\"Exploring better ways for ambitious builders to find the right people, form teams, and build together.\"\n\nSecondary line:\n\n\"Continuing to explore product ideas, full-stack systems, and technology ventures under NAMACO.\"\n\n============================================================\n18 \342\200\224 PERSONAL BRAND / NAMACO CONNECTION\n============================================================\n\nIntroduce NAMACO subtly.\n\nExample:\n\n\"Building with a long-term technology company mindset under NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED.\"\n\nDo not turn the portfolio into a NAMACO corporate website.\n\nThis remains Hassan\'s personal portfolio.\n\n============================================================\n19 \342\200\224 CONTACT\n============================================================\n\nCreate a powerful final CTA.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Let\'s build something meaningful.\"\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"I\'m open to interesting projects, collaborations, product conversations, and opportunities to build.\"\n\nDisplay:\n\nEMAIL\nolamideh825@gmail.com\n\nPHONE\n08051842700\n\nINSTAGRAM\n@namacotechnology\n\nInstagram URL:\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/namacotechnology\n\nUse elegant iconography.\n\nOnly include other social networks when their real URLs are provided.\n\nDo not fabricate GitHub, LinkedIn, X, or other profiles.\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\nSEND AN EMAIL\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\nVIEW INSTAGRAM\n\n============================================================\n20 \342\200\224 FOOTER\n============================================================\n\nFooter:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nPRODUCT BUILDER \302\267 FULL-STACK DEVELOPER \302\267 FOUNDER\n\nBuilding under:\n\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\nFooter navigation:\n\nWORK\nABOUT\nCAPABILITIES\nCONTACT\n\nContact:\n\nolamideh825@gmail.com\n\nPhone:\n\n08051842700\n\nInstagram:\n\n@namacotechnology\n\nAdd:\n\n\302\251 2026 Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide\n\nDo not make the footer unnecessarily large.\n\n============================================================\n21 \342\200\224 MICRO-INTERACTIONS\n============================================================\n\nUse elegant motion.\n\nPreferred:\n- page reveal\n- subtle typography animation\n- smooth scrolling\n- project image reveal\n- card hover states\n- understated image movement\n- navigation transitions\n\nAvoid:\n- excessive particles\n- neon glow\n- bouncing objects\n- giant 3D graphics\n- spinning shapes\n- flashy cursor effects\n- excessive parallax\n\nAnimation should communicate refinement.\n\n============================================================\n22 \342\200\224 RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n============================================================\n\nThe website must be exceptional on:\n\nDESKTOP\nTABLET\nMOBILE\n\nDo not simply collapse desktop into mobile.\n\nMobile must have deliberate:\n- typography\n- spacing\n- navigation\n- image ratios\n- project cards\n- interaction patterns\n- case-study layouts\n\nNo horizontal overflow.\n\nNo broken layouts.\n\nNo tiny unreadable text.\n\n============================================================\n23 \342\200\224 ACCESSIBILITY\n============================================================\n\nImplement:\n\n- semantic HTML\n- keyboard navigation\n- visible focus states\n- correct heading hierarchy\n- accessible buttons\n- descriptive alt text\n- sufficient contrast\n- accessible navigation\n- reduced-motion support\n\n============================================================\n24 \342\200\224 PERFORMANCE\n============================================================\n\nBuild a production-quality website.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- optimized images\n- lazy loading\n- responsive images\n- semantic markup\n- efficient React architecture\n- minimal unnecessary JavaScript\n- fast initial load\n- clean component structure\n- no unnecessary libraries\n- no console errors\n- no broken links\n\n============================================================\n25 \342\200\224 SEO\n============================================================\n\nPage title:\n\nHassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 Product Builder, Full-Stack Developer & Founder\n\nMeta description:\n\n\"Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide is a Nigerian product builder, full-stack developer, and founder building digital products, platforms, and technology experiences.\"\n\nOpen Graph title:\n\nHassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 Product Builder & Founder\n\nOpen Graph description:\n\n\"Digital products, platforms, experiments, and technology experiences built by Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide.\"\n\nUse clean URLs.\n\nExample:\n\n/\n/work\n/work/veyra\n/work/doerly\n/work/tahab-hotel\n/work/split-and-settle\n/about\n/contact\n\n============================================================\n26 \342\200\224 PROJECT CARD DESIGN\n============================================================\n\nProject cards should feel editorial and premium.\n\nEach card should include:\n\nPROJECT NUMBER\n\nPROJECT NAME\n\nCATEGORY\n\nSHORT DESCRIPTION\n\nVISUAL\n\nYEAR\n\nVIEW PROJECT\n\nExample:\n\n01\n\nVEYRA\n\nPRODUCT \302\267 PLATFORM\n\n\"Helping ambitious builders find the right people to build with.\"\n\n2026\n\nVIEW PROJECT \342\206\222\n\nProject images should dominate the card.\n\nUse actual screenshots rather than generic generated illustrations.\n\n============================================================\n27 \342\200\224 VISUAL STORYTELLING\n============================================================\n\nDo not make the website text-heavy.\n\nLet the work speak visually.\n\nUse large:\n- product screenshots\n- browser previews\n- mobile mockups\n- UI crops\n- interface details\n\nFor each important project, create a visual narrative.\n\nThe visitor should be able to understand the quality of the work before reading every paragraph.\n\n============================================================\n28 \342\200\224 PERSONAL POSITIONING\n============================================================\n\nThe portfolio must establish this identity:\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nis not presented merely as:\n\n\"someone learning to code.\"\n\nHe is presented as:\n\nA young technology builder who is actively creating products, learning by building, working with businesses, and developing toward becoming a serious founder.\n\nThis positioning must come from the actual portfolio evidence.\n\nDo NOT fabricate seniority.\n\nDo NOT call Hassan:\n- senior engineer\n- CTO\n- billionaire founder\n- industry leader\n- expert in every technology\n\nunless those claims become factually justified.\n\nAmbition is enough.\n\n============================================================\n29 \342\200\224 FINAL EXPERIENCE\n============================================================\n\nThe visitor\'s mental progression should be:\n\nFIRST:\n\n\"Who is this?\"\n\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\nProduct Builder \302\267 Full-Stack Developer \302\267 Founder\n\nTHEN:\n\n\"What has he actually built?\"\n\nVEYRA\nDOERLY\nTAHAB HOTEL\nSPLIT & SETTLE\nCLIENT WORK\nMORE PROJECTS\n\nTHEN:\n\n\"Does he understand technology?\"\n\nFrontend\nBackend\nDatabase\nAuthentication\nDeployment\nProduct Architecture\n\nTHEN:\n\n\"Does he understand products?\"\n\nProblem\nProduct\nDesign\nEngineering\nShipping\n\nFINALLY:\n\n\"What could he build next?\"\n\nCurrently Building:\nVEYRA\n\nBuilding under:\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\n============================================================\n30 \342\200\224 CRITICAL DESIGN PRINCIPLE\n============================================================\n\nBuild a portfolio where the WORK is the proof.\n\nLess self-promotion.\nMore evidence.\n\nLess:\n\"I\'m passionate about technology.\"\n\nMore:\n\"Here is what I built.\"\n\nLess:\n\"I am a great developer.\"\n\nMore:\n\"Here is the product, architecture, interface, and implementation.\"\n\nLess decoration.\nMore precision.\n\nLess template.\nMore identity.\n\nThe final website must feel:\n\nPREMIUM\nINTELLIGENT\nTECHNICAL\nAMBITIOUS\nCREDIBLE\nEDITORIAL\nHUMAN\nUNMISTAKABLY HASSAN\n\nThe final impression should be:\n\n\"This person is still early in his journey, but he is already building seriously.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"He doesn\'t just write code.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"He thinks about products.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"I want to see what he builds next.\"\n\n============================================================\nFINAL PERSONAL INFORMATION\n============================================================\n\nFULL NAME:\nHASSAN ABDULSATAR OLAMIDE\n\nROLE:\nProduct Builder \302\267 Full-Stack Developer \302\267 Founder\n\nBRAND:\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED\n\nEMAIL:\nolamideh825@gmail.com\n\nPHONE:\n08051842700\n\nINSTAGRAM:\n@namacotechnology\n\nINSTAGRAM URL:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/namacotechnology"
    }
    media {
      mime_type: "image/jpeg"
