  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Files**\n\nI\'ve taken a look at the image files that were just provided. They seem to be crucial elements within the multimodal context, and I\'m gearing up to analyze them to assess their significance.\n\n\n**Creating Logo SVGs**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating precise vector representations of the NAMACO logo. I\'ve broken down the visual components: the geometric \"N\" symbol, the bold \"NAMACO\" text, and the tagline \"TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED.\" My current plan is to craft an exact SVG element, which I\'ll save as `public/namaco-logo.svg` (or a PNG as backup) to ensure crisp rendering.\n\n\n**Reviewing Project Specs**\n\nMy latest thought process involves a thorough review of the project specifications. I\'m double-checking the hero section requirements, specifically focusing on the mandates to avoid stock photography or generated portraits. I must ensure I adhere to the emphasis on oversized typography, grid usage, alignment, restrained animation, elegant whitespace, and detailed metadata. I\'m now cross-referencing this with the proof-of-work section to confirm compliance with all stipulations and mandates.\n\n\n**Defining Brand Identity**\n\nMy focus has shifted to establishing the brand identity. I\'m building under the NAMACO brand, positioning Hassan as a product builder. The core message I\'m formulating is: \"I don\'t just write code. I turn ideas into real digital products,\" which will be delivered without embellishment. I\'m aiming for an editorial technology portfolio look, with a black and white palette, and a premium, intelligent aesthetic. Navigation will include `WORK`, `ABOUT`, `CAPABILITIES`, `CONTACT`, plus a `LET\'S CONNECT` button. The hero section will feature Hassan\'s name, a descriptor, and a compelling headline.\n\n\n**Crafting Section Content**\n\nI\'m now writing supporting copy for the hero section: \"I\'m Hassan Abdulsatar Olamide \342\200\224 a product builder, full-stack developer, and founder focused on turning ideas into useful digital experiences, platforms, and products.\" and a brand affiliation badge. Next, I am drafting the editorial introduction, including the headline \"From idea to interface to product.\" and the accompanying copy: \"I work across product thinking, interface design, frontend development, backend systems, and deployment \342\200\224 bringing ideas from concept to something people can actually use.\" After this, I\'ll flesh out the `SELECTED WORK` section, including project descriptions and case study details for featured projects like VEYRA and DOERLY.\n\n\n**Showcasing Portfolio Items**\n\nI\'m expanding the portfolio to include \'TAHAB HOTEL & SUITES\' and \'SPLIT & SETTLE,\' each with specific category labels, live URLs, and descriptions. For the \'MORE WORK\' section, I\'m organizing a premium project grid with visual hierarchy, and also have a dedicated \'CLIENT & BUSINESS WORK\' section with a supporting statement. I\'ll include several businesses I am working on in this section, accurately labeling their roles.\n\n\n**Implementing Project Filters**\n\nI\'ve been working on the project filtering system. I\'m building out tabs for `ALL`, `PRODUCTS`, `CLIENT WORK`, `WEB APPS`, and `EXPERIMENTS`, ensuring smooth transitions and mobile responsiveness.\n\n**Constructing Case Studies**\n\nI am now focusing on case studies for major projects. I\'m structuring them with a defined layout: overview, problem, idea, product thinking, user experience, design, engineering, key decisions, challenges, outcome, and lessons learned. I\'ll maintain transparency in describing outcomes.\n\n\n\n**Defining My Ambitions**\n\nMy core thought process revolves around what I am trying to build and how. I find immense satisfaction in creating technology that solves genuine issues, which is something I want to do on a global stage from Africa. I enjoy managing the entire product lifecycle and am now establishing a capabilities section showcasing \'PRODUCT\', \'FRONTEND\', \'BACKEND\', and \'FULL-STACK\' proficiencies. Furthermore, I\'ve defined my five-step process: `UNDERSTAND`, `STRUCTURE`, `DESIGN`, `BUILD`, and `SHIP`. I am also including an interactive screenshot gallery.\n\n\n**Detailing Case Study Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating elements for a more engaging case study experience, including interactive interface crops, live code architecture cards, responsive device frames, deployment evidence, and project links. I\'ve also added detail on VEYRA, including copy: \"Exploring better ways for ambitious builders to find the right people, form teams, and build together.\" and a secondary line: \"Continuing to explore product ideas, full-stack systems, and technology ventures under NAMACO.\" Further, I\'m building with a long-term company mindset under NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED and am now implementing the official NAMACO logo. I\'m building out a \"CONTACT\" section with a call to action and contact details, and a dynamic mailto form.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 762744840
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
